---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(&args)
---
Vault an ACH account (POST /v2/payment-methods/ach)

Usage: flute2 payment-methods add-ach [OPTIONS] --account <ACCOUNT_NUMBER> --routing <ROUTING_NUMBER> --account-holder-type <ACCOUNT_HOLDER_TYPE>

Options:
      --account <ACCOUNT_NUMBER>
          Bank account number (required)
      --routing <ROUTING_NUMBER>
          ABA routing number (required)
      --account-type <ACCOUNT_TYPE>
          Account type: `checking` (default) or `savings` [default: checking] [possible values: checking, savings]
      --account-holder-type <ACCOUNT_HOLDER_TYPE>
          Account holder type: `business` or `personal` (required) [possible values: business, personal]
      --tax-id <TAX_ID>
          Tax ID (optional)
      --customer-id <CUSTOMER_ID>
          Customer UUID to vault the account against
      --name <NAME>
          Friendly label for this payment method
      --company-name <COMPANY_NAME>
          Company name, for a business account. With `--customer-id` the customer's company name is used instead and this value is not stored, so a business account needs a company name on the customer
  -h, --help
          Print help

Global options:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Active profile (environment). `sandbox` (default) or `production`/`prod` [env: FLUTE2_PROFILE=]
      --output <OUTPUT>    Output format: table (default), json, or quiet (id only). When omitted, falls back to the `FLUTE2_OUTPUT` env var, then to the `output` key in ~/.flute2/config.toml, then to `table` [env: FLUTE2_OUTPUT=] [possible values: table, json, quiet]
      --debug              Print HTTP request/response traces to stderr. Card and bank-account numbers are masked to the last 4 digits; CVV/security codes are removed
